 "findings": {
  "free_border_vertices": "only lateral thorax | posterior arm (outer L 28, R 20) runs free between two locks; every other chest border with an unchanged region is locked vertex for vertex. Q377 classify \"unjoined\" on pectoral|deltopectoral, epigastric|umbilical, infraclavicular|lateral neck, scapular, hypochondriac are chest vertices made rim by a fold of the sheet within 1.5 mm of the neighbour, not border vertices.",
  "inner_sheet_axilla": "refused: the arm and chest inner sheets diverge 2-5 mm at the axillary fold (chest inner partner to the arm inner border p50 ~3.2 mm), the arm inner rim graph is broken at the anterior|posterior arm corner (gap 17-41 mm), one run would turn faces > 60 deg; the chest wall there stays drawn as before.",
  "corner_deltoid_deltopectoral_infraclavicular": "the 3.6 mm pair: on Base\u00b7F deltoid v301 (L) / v12 (R) is welded to the infraclavicular fossa, the chest-chest border deltopectoral|infraclavicular meets the deltoid border 3.6 mm away; the corner runs (2 L / 3 R vertices incl. the chest-chest corner) need 4.7-5.1 mm moves > cap 4 mm: refused, reported.",
  "sternal_crease": "geometry, not a join: presternal L|R share all 53 midline vertices (welded, engine seam normal = mean of both sides within 0.9 deg p50); the two halves meet at 30.6 deg p50 / 49.1 p95 (within a half 2.7 deg p50) -- the sternal furrow of the Z source (Base\u00b7M: -46..-58 deg V over 2-12 mm, deeper than Base\u00b7F -16..-25; Base\u00b7F before Q360 similar). Q360 shipped no chest-to-chest walls, but no wall belongs on a shared surface border; re-running Q360 with --chest-walls would refit the whole chest and could not remove a V that is in its target; the missing walls were added here instead (no refit) -- they fix the open slot of a hidden region, not the crease.",
  "lower_edge_band": "not a join, wall or crease: epigastric|umbilical and hypochondriac|lateral abdomen are locked vertex for vertex, all chest walls there twinned and hidden; dihedral across the border 7.2 deg p50 (Base\u00b7M 7.1); normal tilt step chest->abdomen 7.5 deg (Base\u00b7M 7.6). What differs is the Q360 fitted surface itself: face-normal sd 4.5 deg in the 2-15 mm band above the border (Base\u00b7M 0.7) -- the ripple of the fit, 2.7 mm edges against the 18.5 mm edges of the unchanged abdomen. Remedy is a re-fit (out of scope).",
  "axillary_step_r": "not touched (6 vertices of anterior_region_of_arm_r 16-44 mm in front of the smooth map wrap breast_ct_r 2 mm under the skin); a guarded option would need a joint re-fit of the arm slab with the chest around breast_ct_r with the breast tuck guard (Q353) -- not a border move.",
  "under_skin_recounted": "latissimus dorsi L/R (1 vertex each, 10.5 / 11.4 mm out) and long head of triceps L (2) / R (1) (0.6-1.0 mm out) lie outside the skin before AND after at the same height; outside_count skipped them before because they lay over the gap/overlap at the axillary border (its \"covered\" test). Pre-existing, now counted.",
  "chest_walls": "added (--chest-walls): 3920 triangles on the 18 chest slabs along every chest-to-chest border (Q360 slab rule, no refit, no vertex moved); engine (node, final page): 3920/3920 hidden as twins while both regions are drawn; hiding one region now shows its neighbour's wall instead of an open slot. Seam normals change only at chest seam vertices, most at the 76 deg deltopectoral|pectoral fold (up to 56 deg at 7 vertices), elsewhere <= 6 deg."
 },
